    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF146 adds support for using non-registered symbols as keys for WeakMap and values for WeakSet in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1966745\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1966745</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The issue only talks about WeakMap, but I ran a test for WeakSet and that behaves the same way:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"const ws = new WeakSet();\nconst sym = Symbol('foo');\nws.add(sym); \"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">ws</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">WeakSet</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">sym</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">Symbol</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'foo'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">ws</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">add</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">sym</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span> </pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the subfeature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3607691670\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41868\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41868/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41868\">mdn/content#41868</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28498",
            "title": "FF146 WeakMap/WeakSet use non-registered symbols as keys/values",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-21T04:01:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-21T04:00:38.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF146 supports WebCrypto import of EC keys in compressed format in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1971499\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1971499</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've added as a subfeature of importKey</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3607703023\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41870\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41870/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41870\">mdn/content#41870</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28497",
            "title": "FF146 EC compressed data supported on import of EC key",
            "date_modified": "2025-11-21T01:56:06.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-11-21T01:54:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107345594?u=dd2534c29da0184e6446eb1e7c6be0412ea3c489&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR corrects the compatibility data for <code class=\"notranslate\">navigator.share()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">navigator.canShare()</code> (specifically <code class=\"notranslate\">data_text_parameter</code>) in Firefox and Firefox for Android.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Changes applied:</strong></p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Firefox (Desktop):</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Restored version:</strong> Restored <code class=\"notranslate\">version_added: \"96\"</code> which appears to have been inadvertently removed in PR <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2393967818\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23687\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23687/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23687\">#23687</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Added flag:</strong> Added the <code class=\"notranslate\">dom.webshare.enabled</code> flag configuration to accurately reflect that this feature requires a preference setting.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Firefox for Android:</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Mirror removal:</strong> Switched from <code class=\"notranslate\">\"mirror\"</code> to explicit version numbers (<code class=\"notranslate\">\"71\"</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">share</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">\"96\"</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">canShare</code>) to bypass the flag requirement issue.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Context and Verification:</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Mirroring Issue:</strong> Currently, the desktop <code class=\"notranslate\">firefox</code> entry requires the <code class=\"notranslate\">dom.webshare.enabled</code> preference. However, <code class=\"notranslate\">firefox_android</code> is defined with <code class=\"notranslate\">\"accepts_flags\": false</code>. Consequently, the build script incorrectly resolves the mirrored support status to <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Android <code class=\"notranslate\">canShare</code> status:</strong> There appear to have been historical bugs regarding <code class=\"notranslate\">data_text_parameter</code> support in <code class=\"notranslate\">canShare</code> on Android. Although I was unable to trace the specific details or issue tracks myself, I have confirmed on a physical device (latest Firefox for Android) that it currently works as expected.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2393967818\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23687\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23687/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/23687\">#23687</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1066775100\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/13810\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/13810/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/13810\">#13810</a></li>\n</ul>",
